00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
apple's m1 mac mini has been completely  changing the personal computing game  since it was released a couple of months  back at just 699 dollars  it offers the absolute best bang for the  buck that you can get  if you want a mac machine or maybe even  better than a diy  windows pc now they might sound a bit  unrealistic  but i'll explain my reasoning in just a  minute in this long term review  i want to discuss the major benefits as  well as the issues  with the m1 mac mini because it's  definitely  not perfect and at the end i'm going to  discuss  who shouldn't buy the m1 mac mini and  why  but first let me give you a quick  rundown on this machine and why i think  there is  so much value in it the design is very  sleek and compact  compared to most computers out there  with a premium aluminum finish  around back you get some ports including  two thunderbolt ports  two usb a hdmi 2.0 ethernet  and of course a headphone jack the  entire system is cooled by just one  fan but because of the extremely  efficient apple m1 chip  it never runs loud enough to hear it  even while running performance tasks  the reason for that is because this ship  is the first of its kind  while most traditional computer chips  are built on the x86  architecture this one is built on  apple's arm-based architecture  that they've been working on for years  now it's basically a  souped-up iphone or ipad chip but with  added components that help make it a  fully capable computer  like the io chip the thunderbolt  controllers and more  and because it shares the same core  architecture as an iphone  it can actually run your favorite iphone  apps  which wasn't possible before mac apps  run great as well  even ones that haven't been updated for  these new chips  and in our experience this m1 mac mini  feels more snappy  than our 15 000 mac pro for day-to-day  work  for example some apps like audacity and  photoshop  open around twice as fast on the mini  which was completely unexpected  and if you're wondering how that's  possible it's because apple's m1 chip  has an incredibly high single core score  in fact the highest out of any mac ever  but it's not just single core the  multi-core performance is also  incredibly high outperforming the  absolute best chip  in the previous intel mac mini so as you  can tell  the value is definitely there but the  even more impressive part is the  performance of apple's built-in 8-core  graphics chip  it absolutely destroys the previous best  graphics performance in the intel mac  mini  being over 4 times as fast and that's  because the mac mini is way too small  and compact  to be able to fit a dedicated graphics  card or chip  so mac minis have always suffered in  terms of graphics performance  but now that problem is solved thanks to  apple's new m1 chip  and the performance we're getting is  very similar to the base  5300 5300m graphics in this 16-inch  macbook pro  which is really impressive for  integrated graphics  so with the combination of a premium and  compact design  the very reliable mac os software and  very impressive performance  you're truly getting a lot of value for  700  and because of that i want to focus a  lot of this review  comparing the value aspect to other  machines  in its price range let's just say you  have a parent or a relative  who needs a basic computer to browse the  web  do some business or school related work  or anything like that  i strongly believe that the m1 mac mini  is the absolute best choice a similarly  priced intel nok is gonna have much  lower performance  just like intel's mac mini a pre-built  pc like this one  for a similar price is first of all very  large  the fans are gonna run loud and it's  gonna run much  slower so compared to those pre-built  machines  the m1 mac mini is a far better deal so  i took it to the next level  a few months back we made a video where  we built a custom gaming pc  with the goal of it being the best  budget gaming pc  right now the components for the build  come out to over 700 dollars in total  more than the m1 mac mini but keep in  mind that we had to spend a few hours  building it troubleshooting and setting  it up the ryzen 3100 cpu is known as one  of the best bank for the bug  processors but the m1 chip is still  around  37 faster in terms of the cinebench r23  stress test  the rx 560 graphics card is actually  weaker than the m1s graphics  in terms of gfx bench so the mac mini  is still more powerful in every way and  those are actually some of the best  value budget components that we can find  right now we even had to cheap out on  basically everything else  like the case the motherboard the power  supply  and the ssd to get the price anywhere  near the m1 mac mini  and that's even without paying for a  windows 10 license  while the mac obviously gets mac os for  free so as you can see  basically every windows system that you  can get right now  is a much worse value than the m1 mac  mini but besides that  this mac is a whole lot more reliable  because apple controls both the software  and the hardware so it works extremely  well together  and gives you incredible reliability  with windows machines  you usually have a bunch of different  third-party components  working together and those parts are  much more likely to go bad  and have software issues with different  drivers and things like that  but on the other hand the mac mini is  very similar to a pc  since you can pick and choose the mouse  the keyboard  and the display that you use with it and  having the freedom to choose whatever  component you want  can really help bring the price down if  you're on a budget  so based on everything that i discussed  the m1 mac mini ultimately gives you  excellent performance and reliability  for the price  making it in my opinion the new standard  for a personal desktop computer however  while it is great  it's definitely not perfect so let's get  into some of the issues that we  experience with it the biggest issue is  a lack of ports  with the m1 mac mini only offering two  thunderbolt ports  instead of the previous maximum of four  so this means that if you're using a  display that  uses thunderbolt like we do here in the  office  you only have one thunderbolt port left  and because the m1 mac mini doesn't have  an  option for a 10 gigabit ethernet port we  had to use the other thunderbolt port  for our raid storage server now for most  people this isn't a big deal at all  because a lot of people use  hdmi displays leaving the two  thunderbolt ports left  over and most people don't use server  storage  as well those ports are mostly just for  accessories  so it's totally fine since you also have  two  extra usb a ports as well but for that  one person who really needs  more than two thunderbolt ports we found  the perfect solution to the problem  owc's new thunderbolt hub literally  turns  one thunderbolt port into three and then  adds an extra usb a port for  a hundred and fifty dollars so while  that isn't cheap  it's the only way to get extra full  speed thunderbolt ports  this can also help fix the problem of  limited displays  with the m1 chip only being able to  support two displays total  if you're someone who really needs more  than two displays  there are many people out there who have  been connecting up to six displays  to m1 max using hardware adapters and  special software  with really good results so that's great  to hear one of the issues we've been  experiencing is bluetooth connection  problems  but we've really only noticed it with  third party accessories  we used our m1 mac mini with apple's  magic mouse  and had basically no issues but now  apple has just released an update  that improves bluetooth reliability and  users are reporting that the issues seem  to be  finally fixed with one user going two  days  without a disconnect now another one of  the problems that people had  was with video editing people reported  that the encoding quality was worse on  n1 max  compared to previous intel max but we  ended up doing some in-depth testing  and found that the m1s encode it better  than apple's mac pro  which basically shows that it's just  fine so there are no  issues there another problem we had was  with certain plugins  not being supported on apple silicon max  like  m callouts which we use in a lot of our  videos  as of right now most plugins have been  updated to support apple silicon  but there are still some plugins that  are outdated but  thankfully we found a solution on the m  callouts faq section  you can run a script for either final  cut pro or motion  which will force it to run using rosetta  thus allowing those plug-ins to run  again and the performance under rosetta  is still  very fast so those were the main issues  that we've been experiencing  and a lot of them have either been fixed  or have easy solutions to them  and most of them don't even matter to  the average consumer who just needs a  reliable computer  and now if you combine the performance  the efficiency and the reliability  you're truly getting a ton of value for  the cash  especially compared to other desktop  windows pcs that you can get right now  and because of all of that i've got to  say that the m1 mac mini  is by far the best computer to buy for  someone looking for a budget pc  right now but with all of that said  there are actually still some people  who should not buy an m1 mac mini so  let's get into that  if this m1 seems a bit limiting in terms  of the performance or anything else  we are expecting apple to release a more  powerful m1x mac mini in the future  potentially even later this year so keep  that in mind  on top of that we're already expecting a  new imac  coming out within the next few months so  if you don't already have a keyboard  a mouse and a display on hand the imac  will  be a better value if you want a high  quality display  but if the performance of the m1 is  enough for you  then i would totally just buy the m1 mac  mini right now  and enjoy a reliable value computer for  the next five plus years  so there you guys go hopefully you  enjoyed this review and if you did go  ahead and tap the like button  and click the circle above to subscribe  for more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  videos right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in  the next video

